WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.039 --> 00:00:07.206
- Riding a blind horse,
that's a little different.

00:00:08.145 --> 00:00:11.932
But to me it don't make much difference.

00:00:11.932 --> 00:00:14.543
He's a pretty good friend.

00:00:14.543 --> 00:00:18.010
He’s just tickled to death to be rode.

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:20.046
I think he knows that he got eyes then,

00:00:20.046 --> 00:00:21.474
and he just jumps up and down

00:00:21.474 --> 00:00:24.141
and runs and really likes to go.

00:00:28.565 --> 00:00:33.165
My name's Roderick Olsen,
in Soldier Grove, Wisconsin.

00:00:33.165 --> 00:00:36.186
I have always had a few
horses, matter of fact,

00:00:36.186 --> 00:00:38.227
quite a few of them.

00:00:38.227 --> 00:00:41.980
Well, we got Zaxson about 21 years ago,

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:46.055
about 10 years ago that we
noticed that he was going blind.

00:00:46.055 --> 00:00:49.552
Far as we could find out,
nothing we could do about it.

00:00:49.552 --> 00:00:52.120
Most of the old horse dealers,
or farmers, they'd just

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.870
get rid of the horse.

00:00:56.274 --> 00:00:58.474
But I figured I'd then keep him.

00:00:58.474 --> 00:01:00.524
I'd like to stick around a while longer,

00:01:00.524 --> 00:01:04.691
so if I went blind, I hope
they'd keep me around a while.

00:01:08.109 --> 00:01:10.692
I didn't figure he was useless.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:15.852
He does everything you want
by the feel of the reins.

00:01:15.852 --> 00:01:20.043
He's a little different
riding than a regular horse.

00:01:20.043 --> 00:01:22.448
He's careful when he's running,

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:24.850
you know he ain't sure
where his feet's going to go

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:27.620
or what's in front of him.
But he didn't just quit

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.678
because he got blind,

00:01:28.678 --> 00:01:32.545
he's trying to do things so
he can take care of himself.

00:01:32.545 --> 00:01:34.628
He trusts me to ride him.

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:38.977
I think he just figures
that man I can see now.

00:01:38.977 --> 00:01:40.156
I got eyes.

00:01:40.156 --> 00:01:43.661
I can do things that I
wanted to do for a long time.

00:01:43.661 --> 00:01:45.411
He wants to just run.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:49.980
He's fun for me to ride.

00:01:50.829 --> 00:01:53.066
We go all over the
hills, down the canyons,

00:01:53.066 --> 00:01:57.703
in the water, everywhere
that any other horse can go.

00:01:57.703 --> 00:01:59.203
He does just fine.

00:02:00.471 --> 00:02:04.258
He must trust me and, well, I trust him.

00:02:04.258 --> 00:02:06.701
He's kind of a buddy anyhow.

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:09.184
Being friends with a horse, that’s a, I don't know

00:02:09.184 --> 00:02:12.934
that's the way it's been
with me all my life.

